>> >> Err... it's not as easy as that I'm afraid.  Distance does
>> >> post-stratification before sending the data off to the analysis engines.
>> >>  So, the analysis engine would see two strata (left and right), with lines
>> >> within each strata, and it would bootstrap the lines within strata
>> >> independently, which is not what is wanted here.  I'm afraid the only way I
>> >> know of to take account of the dependence is to program a bootstrap outside
>> >> of the Distance interface - something about which there are several postings
>> >> already on the list.  On the plus side, ignoring the dependence will result
>> >> in an overestimate of variance, and an overestimate is better than an
>> >> underestimate...
>> >>
>> >> I wonder why one would want a separate estimate for each side of a survey
>> >> platform in the first place.  If it's to account for observer differences in
>> >> detection prob, one can do this by having observer or side as covariates in
>> >> the mcds or mrds analysis engines. I expect I'm missing something obvious
>> >> here...
>> >>
>> >>  - Len Thomas
