Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2009 16:33:11 +0000
Subject: Re: Occupancy vs. DS ?
Message-ID: <1Jm8_qyDpAk.7cweIgci8ggJ@distance-sampling.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <1Jm8_qyDpAk.mU645wldjpcJ@distance-sampling.groups.google.com>
References: <1Jm8_qyDpAk.mU645wldjpcJ@distance-sampling.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/distance-sampling/c/1Jm8_qyDpAk/m/7cweIgci8ggJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Occupancy simply converts abundance to 0/1 and can be defined for an
area although I'm not sure it always is in applications.  It uses
multiple visits or multiple methods with some fairly strong assumptions
to assess detection probability.  Usually requires 5-6 visits.  I can
see it working well for relatively sedentary critters like amphibians,
or territorial birds and with well-defined or possibly discrete sites
(e.g, ponds).

--jeff

